# xrpchange.site — out of scope by default

Unless the user **explicitly** names **xrpchange** / **xrpchange.site** in the **current** request, treat that stack as **not part of this work**.

## Do not (without explicit user direction)

- Configure, debug, deploy, test, or document **`*.xrpchange.site`** API/Core.
- Commit or deploy **`.env.xrpchange`** (gitignored; local second-server sim only — use **`.env.xrpchange.example`** in repo).
- Edit **`docs/ENV_XRPCHANGE.md`** or xrpchange-only vhost/CORS unless the user explicitly asks about local dual-exchange dev.
- Assume local Apache serves `sandbox.api.xrpchange.site` for the user’s current task.
- Curl or migrate against xrpchange DB/env “by default”.

## Default API on this project

- **`api.xdexboard.com`**, **`sandbox.api.xdexboard.com`**, **`dev.api.xdexboard.com`** → **`.env`** (VAPID, DB, Core URLs the user maintains there).
- Cross-repo docs and client calls should match **xdexboard** hostnames unless the user says otherwise.
